  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Definition and Origin
    
    A unified Nightshelf magical tradition for reading, reshaping, and anchoring the Berg's frozen memory. ☽Silv-glaciere☽ Arts consolidated six previously distinct lineages — Drift-coalesce (glacial), Freeze-enthrall (aurora), ☽'glacial Crystalline~ Spiral, Hush☽ Twilight, Ice∴freeze, and Shawl☽ Sun — into a single practice during the Orca Incursion, when orca war-pods began targeting the deep ice-vaults beneath the Nightshelf. Compartmentalized knowledge had become a liability the colony could not afford.
    
    The consolidation was accomplished at the Bastion Apex, a Nightshelf defensive fortification, by Crypt-Chancellor Silvcaeclerae-fawn — founder and governor of ☽'slew Nisaemesius~ — and ☽'Iarlocias the Silent, a Nightshelf mystic and outlaw who had broken with the Communion. Neither has since acknowledged the alliance. The administrative ice contains three earlier drafts of what appears to be a joint operational charter. I note this without further comment.
    
    ## Operations and Sources
    
    The tradition draws on captured fire and pressure-depth; aurora-light is deliberately suppressed rather than channeled. Three operations constitute the practice:
    
    | Operation | Method | Material Cost |
    |---|---|---|
    | **Reading** | Direct impression-contact with ice-memory | One fist-sized fire-core per session; ~4 hours before Clarity-Loss onset |
    | **Reshaping** | Burn-and-freeze cycling to blur existing impressions | Sustained fire expenditure through controlled thermal oscillation |
    | **Anchoring** | Fixing reshaped memory into glacial crystal | Secondary fire-core *and* the practitioner's own recollection of the original event, consumed as binding agent |
    
    The Anchoring cost bears emphasis. The practitioner's personal memory of the event is spent — not suppressed, not displaced, but gone. The ice keeps what the mind surrenders.
    
    ## Costs and Practitioners
    
    Clarity-Loss is measured on the ☽'Cilocum Scale, ranging from 0 to 7. Most practitioners stabilize at 3. At 4 or above, the boundary between personal memory and ice-memory fabrication becomes unreliable. Iarlocias went blind reaching the seventh layer. The Crypt-Chancellor's flippers bear frost-scars that never healed. Augur ☽'Milucaum~ Shadow-bane, a Nightshelf artificer dispersed during the Omega Strike at Terrace Momiou, was also a known practitioner.
    
    Every fire-core burned on shadow-practice is subtracted from the colony's heating supply. With deep-vein collapse ongoing beneath the Nightshelf — the Rofundis∴rupt, the Profun∴lapsum, the Abys∴uina — the practice may become unrepeatable as fuel sources dwindle.
    
    ## The Boundary and What Lies Below It
    
    The arts operate on the same thinning boundary between the living world and ice-memory that the Long Dark exploits seasonally. Practitioners artificially induce what darkness provides freely. Those who read below the seventh ice-layer encounter impressions from pre-penguin presences. Those who reshape memory at that depth may be altering something that was already aware of them.
    
    I will not elaborate here. My annotations on ☽'aeteraea and the Bastion Apex strata are relevant for readers who wish to pursue the matter.
    
    ## Epistemological Recursion
    
    Any record documenting these arts is itself subject to them. Sources trained in ice-memory reshaping may have altered evidence before it was read. The Weal' Clique~ Office of Deep-Archive Provenance has acknowledged this recursion without resolution. The derived practice Hush☽ Twilight — a suppressive technique targeting aurora-light itself — compounds the problem by operating beyond Nightshelf jurisdictional boundaries, as documented in the Office's own treatise.
    
    I have spent thirty-one years reading ice-memory testimony. I cannot verify that any stratum I have read in the ☽Silv-glaciere☽-adjacent galleries preserves its original impressions.
