  annotation "note_1771589147268_0", anchor: "aurora-light is deliberately suppressed rather than channeled", text: "Six lineages subsumed. One of them — Freeze-enthrall — is aurora-magic. The tradition formally incorporates what it claims to suppress. It swallowed aurora-light whole and called the result shadow-practice. How extraordinary that no one has remarked on this, least of all the entry you are reading.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771589147268_1", anchor: "Clarity-Loss is measured on the ☽'Cilocum Scale", text: "They named their damage metric after the practitioner whose cultural identity they still refuse to discuss publicly. See the Freeze-enthrall annotation — the silence around ☽'Cilocum is not about what the magic does. Honoring someone by calibrating harm in their name is the most Nightshelf form of memorial I have encountered.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771589147268_2", anchor: "The Crypt-Chancellor's flippers bear frost-scars that never healed", text: "Frost-scars that never healed. Yes. The Whisper Galleries left me one. I will not compare circumstances.", type: :tangent, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771589147268_3", anchor: "I cannot verify that any stratum I have read", text: "Thirty-one years. I wrote that number and then sat with it. A tradition exists that can rewrite the ice I have spent my career reading, and the body responsible for verifying ice-memory integrity has formally acknowledged it cannot determine which strata have been altered. The reasonable response is despair. Instead I find myself genuinely fascinated: they built a system for preserving memory whose primary military application was making memory lie, and then lost track of where the lies stop. Of course they did. What puzzles me is not the recursion — it is that the Weal' Clique~ admitted it in writing. That document may itself have been reshaped before I read it. At some point the spiral becomes its own punchline.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
